<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 11 December, from 1282 to 1941.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1282</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd, last native Prince of Wales, is killed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd was killed near Cilmeri during Edward I's conquest of Wales. Wales lost its independence, and in 1301 Edward gave the title Prince of Wales to his own son.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1688</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James II flees London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As William of Orange advanced, James II slipped out of Whitehall and dropped the Great Seal into the Thames. Caught at Faversham, he escaped to France later that month; Parliament treated his flight as abdication.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1792</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XVI goes on trial before the National Convention</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The deposed king, now called Louis Capet, appeared before the National Convention to answer charges of treason. He was convicted and guillotined in January 1793.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1936</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward VIII abdicates to marry Wallis Simpson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The abdication took legal effect, and that evening Edward broadcast that he could not reign 'without the help and support of the woman I love'. His brother succeeded as George VI.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1941</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany and Italy declare war on the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four days after Pearl Harbor, Hitler and Mussolini declared war on the United States. The decision brought American power fully into the war in Europe.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></li></ol>
